        {
          "type": "tip",
          "source": "CadillacForums.com",
          "content": "Same LSY 2.0T turbo as XT4. GM Turbocharger Coolant Feed Pipe (12691901) plus gasket (55504552) are the primary failure points. Inspect at every oil change for coolant weeping around turbo area. Replace preventively at 60,000 miles",
          "upvotes": 50,
          "needsReview": false
        },
        {
          "type": "tip",
          "source": "CadillacForums.com",
          "content": "GM PCV Valve 55514392 is the same LSY-specific part across all applications (CT4, XT4, Equinox, Malibu). PCV failure symptoms: excessive oil consumption, check engine light, boost pressure codes. Relatively inexpensive part ($30-50) but labor can be $200+ at dealer",
          "upvotes": 46,
          "needsReview": false
        },
        {
          "type": "tip",
          "source": "CadillacForums.com",
          "content": "5,000-mile oil change intervals with dexos1 Gen 3 0W-20 are critical for LSY turbo longevity. Monthly coolant level checks catch turbo coolant line leaks early. The CT4-V Blackwing uses a different engine (LF4 3.6TT) and is NOT affected by these LSY-specific issues",
          "upvotes": 55,
          "needsReview": false
        },
